license: MIT
abstract: >-
  causalbase learns the structure of Bayesian networks from data. It
  implements greedy equivalence search (GES) and XGES with BDeu, BIC or
  Gaussian BIC, iterated local search over variable orders, FLOP, hill
  climbing and tabu search over DAGs, and exact search by dynamic programming
  or integer programming. Scores and graph routines are compiled with Numba.
  Structural metrics, XMLBIF input, forward sampling and five benchmark
  networks are included. fedcausal, which learns from data split across sites,
  is built on it.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - greedy equivalence search
  - BDeu
  - order search
